# Intent: The inputs the grid games were missing. A finger is classified when it lifts as a tap, a long press (still for 450 ms) or a swipe in four directions (the unit's swipe rule), by a pure core with a host test. The gesture layer learns a flag, MGS_F_GAME_VERT, that a running game sets when it takes vertical swipes inside its play area (2048, Snake): a swipe down there no longer stops the game; only the bottom edge, the grabber at the top and the stop word do, and a swipe up opens no sheet during a game. Games that do not set the flag behave as before. Mine Finder now acts on the lift: a tap opens a cell, a long press flags it (the flag switch stays).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: Mine Finder: a short tap opens a cell, holding half a second flags it, the right-hand switch still turns taps into flags; every other game still stops with a swipe down from anywhere (no game sets the flag yet); the stop word and the grabber still end Mine Finder.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: none (a few hundred bytes of flash; four bytes in the Grid struct).

